   "cardPlace": "Bautzen",
   "summary": "Father of Christa Kohlmann and Sigrid Michaelis.",
   "story": "Father of Christa Kohlmann and Sigrid Michaelis. Thomas Kohlmann's maternal grandfather. Fabrikant: sole proprietor (Inhaber) of Stahldrahtmatratzen-Fabrik Weickert & Eifler, the steel wire mattress factory based in Bautzen, with offices at Martin-Mutschmann-Straße 19 (a Nazi-period street name) and a factory on the Industriegelände Singwitz served by a private rail siding at Gnaschwitz. The firm name preserves a founding partner Weickert who was no longer active by the 1930s; circumstances of Weickert's exit unknown. Documented as proprietor in two surviving company papers: an undated advertising letterhead (1933–1945) and a business invoice dated 9 April 1943. Married Gertrud Elise Becker on 2 October 1926 in Dresden (the chart types 'Dresdan', a typo). Twelve years older than her at marriage. Died of a Schädelbasisbruch (basilar skull fracture) in a car accident, aged 76. Had three siblings on the chart: brothers Max and Alfred and sister Martha (no further details on page 1). Rufname underlined on the chart was 'Alwin', and Documents B and C confirm he went by Alwin in business.[^2007-eifler-becker-ahnentafel-page-1-weickert-eifler-letterh]",
